I think you can manually specify the chromosome names using the "chr" argument in the cset2band() function call.  The syntax will be a bit confusing because in your example "chr" is also the variable name for the chromLoc object.

banded <- cset2band(exprs=exprs,genome=chr,chr=c(1:22,"X","Y"),FUN=mean,na.rm=TRUE)

This will hopefully bypass the more cryptic names in the chromLoc object and help move the process along.

