From naomi at stat.psu.edu  Wed Jun 30 22:53:40 2010
From: naomi at stat.psu.edu (Naomi Altman)
Date: Wed, 30 Jun 2010 16:53:40 -0400
Subject: [BioC] P>1 (edgeR and sage.test)
Message-ID: <6.2.3.4.2.20100630165124.0254e7d0@imap.stat.psu.edu>

Both the Fisher exact test and sage.test (in sagenhaft) can produce 
p-values slightly bigger than 1.  This can mess up down-stream 
analyses (like using qvalue, e.g.). Perhaps the functions could be 
modified to truncate the p-values at 1.0.

